[E0486] Error: a template's `refusal` takes the literal's text and which holes are joined
    ╭─[ err/680_a_refusal_that_takes_no_literal/main.wip:18:12 ]
    │
 18 │     static fn refusal(pieces: &[str]): Option<Refusal> = .None
    │               ───┬───
    │                  ╰───── not what a literal says
    │
    │ Help: declare it `static fn refusal(pieces: &[str], joined: &[bool]): Option<Refusal>`
    │
    │ Note: the compiler asks a template's `refusal` of each literal that builds it, while the program is compiled, and passes it the literal's text between its holes and which holes are of the template's own type
────╯
